                <!-- Census Checks / Coding / Deceased -->
                <tr>
                    <td class="rule-num">34</td><td class="rule-cat">Census Checks</td>
                    <td class="rule-text">Calculate fields used to define census dates:
1. DAYS
a) Calculate the number of days between the First and the Last Class Date.
b) Save the field as c_Days.

2. DAYS_2
a) Calculate the midpoint by dividing the results in 1. by 2 i.e., c_Days/2.
b) Save the field as c_Days_2.

3. CENSUS_DATE_PREP
a) Determine the census date based on adding the results in 2. above to the first lecture date i.e., First_Day_Class + c_Days_2.
b) Save the field as c_Census_Date_Prep.

4. CENSUS_DATE
a) Determine the actual census date based on the results in 3 and if the day falls on a weekend or holiday, the next day or Monday will be the census date.
b) Save the field as c_ACTUAL_CENSUS_DATE.

5. Verify the defined census date against the computed census date i.e., c_ACTUAL_CENSUS_DATE &lt;&gt; s_CENSUS_DATE.</td>
                    <td class="rule-note">No exceptions were identified</td>
                    <td class="rule-script">Refer to Census Date</td>
